# Blender model import and animation runtime

Status: DONE
Milestone: M2 interoperability
Dependencies: 03_BODY_FACE_TRACKING.todo, 11_REFERENCE_AVATAR.todo, 12_PERSPECTIVE_LAB.todo

## Purpose
Prepare TrickRoom to import prepared Blender-exported characters and drive their skinning,
facial morphs, bone motion, materials and supported animation clips.

## Tasks
- [x] Define versioned GLB/humanoid/profile contract and verify upstream export/skinning specs.
- [x] Implement bounded import, diagnostics, node/skin/morph/material/texture/clip support.
- [x] Implement hierarchy-preserving retargeting, visibility, calibration and pose/clip previews.
- [x] Integrate transactional model selection and rendering in UI/CLI without removing built-in avatar.
- [x] Prove behavior and rejection paths with tests and actual exported content.

## Acceptance criteria
- [x] Actual Blender export animates correctly in TrickRoom, including expressions and textures.
- [x] Unsupported features and malformed imports fail explicitly; no raw camera output.
- [x] Existing camera, avatar, room and lifecycle behavior is preserved.

## Completion evidence
-148tests/no skips; original12native groups plus9model UI groups; actual Blender numerical,
  eye-bone/morph/texture/clip, standalone CLI and imported-model stream checks passed.
- API contract and limits are in docs\12-blender-models.md and the82page handbook.
- One clean-output redraw starvation was diagnosed and corrected with a minimum Tk yield;
  the bounded native model check then completed. No owner-camera or universal Blender claim.

